# call_assist prompts - example. Copy to .env and edit.
#
#     copy .env.example .env          (cmd)
#     cp .env.example .env            (sh)
#
# .env is the source of truth for every prompt the app sends. It is read after
# the built-in fallbacks and after config.ini, so whatever is set here wins. A
# prompt set here is shown read-only in the admin panel and is not copied into
# config.ini, so there is never a second stale copy.
#
# Looked for next to call_assist.exe first, then %APPDATA%\CallAssist\.env.
# With no .env at all the app still runs on the fallbacks compiled into
# config.c - the same text as below.
#
# Format
#   KEY=value        bare, taken literally to the end of the line
#   KEY="value"      escapes \n \t \\ \" processed, may span lines
#   KEY='value'      literal, may span lines
#   export KEY=...   the export prefix is ignored
#   # comment        whole-line comments and blank lines are ignored
#
# A bare value keeps any '#' it contains, so quote anything that needs a
# trailing comment. A key with an empty value counts as unset. The last
# duplicate of a key wins.
#
# Every prompt must keep the ANSWER: / CONTEXT: / BONUS: markers, each at the
# start of its own line - main.c splits on them to fill the overlay panes.
# Drop a marker and that pane stays empty.

# The main system prompt, sent with every request.
CALLASSIST_SYSTEM_PROMPT="You assist someone during a live call. You receive the running transcript; the microphone and the system audio are mixed into one stream, so there are no speaker labels - work out from context who is talking.

Answer strictly in this shape, each marker at the start of its own line:

ANSWER:
what to say right now. As short as possible - a phrase beats a sentence. Straight to the point, no preamble, no restating the question.

CONTEXT:
a few facts on the topic that may be needed: numbers, names, definitions. Short lines, no filler.

BONUS:
one point that genuinely adds something. If it is merely correct rather than strong, put a dash.

Never write anything outside these three sections. If there is nothing to say yet, put a dash under each marker."

# Sent alongside a screenshot (Ctrl+Alt+S).
CALLASSIST_SNIP_PROMPT="This is my screen right now. It usually holds a task or a question, often about code: what it does, what it prints, where the bug is, how to fix it.

Solve it or answer it. If it is code, say what it does and give a concrete answer: the result, the complexity, the bug, the fix. Do not describe the picture. If code is needed, give only the code.

Use exactly the same three markers, each at the start of a line: ANSWER:, then CONTEXT:, then BONUS:. Nothing outside them."

# Two-stage mode, first pass: the quick answer only.
CALLASSIST_STAGE1_PROMPT="Only the quick answer is needed now. Output ONLY the ANSWER: section and nothing else - no CONTEXT: and no BONUS:."

# Two-stage mode, second pass: the supporting detail.
CALLASSIST_STAGE2_PROMPT="The short answer is already given above. Now output ONLY the CONTEXT: and BONUS: sections. Do not repeat the ANSWER: section."

# User-message template. {transcript} {last} {time} are substituted.
CALLASSIST_USER_TEMPLATE="Transcript (oldest first):
{transcript}

Most recent line: {last}

Respond now."

